{"E:\\videos\\clyde7\\wt\\vlog\\clyde7\\voz\\b009_t4.wav": {"text": "A small clean fire, 250 degrees, and thin blue smoke. Folks build a big fire, choke it down, and pour white smoke over the meat for six hours. That thick white smoke tastes like an ashtray. It is the number one reason home barbecue tastes bitter. You want smoke you can barely see. Thin, almost blue, coming out the top like a whisper. So get your smoker to 250 degrees and hold it right there. Hickory or oak. Down here we use hickory, the same wood my granddaddy cut off this land. One or two chunks at a time, about the size of your fist, never a whole pile. Let the fire breathe. Keep the vents open. If the smoke comes out thick and white, you have too much wood or not enough air. Open it up and wait until it thins out before the meat goes in. Put the roast on the grate, fat side up, the thickest end toward the fire.", "words": [{"w": " A", "s": 0.0, "e": 0.24}, {"w": " small", "s": 0.24, "e": 0.52}, {"w": " clean", "s": 0.52, "e": 0.94}, {"w": " fire,", "s": 0.94, "e": 2.4}, {"w": " 250", "s": 2.4, "e": 3.18}, {"w": " degrees,", "s": 3.18, "e": 4.8}, {"w": " and", "s": 4.8, "e": 4.94}, {"w": " thin", "s": 4.94, "e": 5.3}, {"w": " blue", "s": 5.3, "e": 5.6}, {"w": " smoke.", "s": 5.6, "e": 6.6}, {"w": " Folks", "s": 7.24, "e": 7.5}, {"w": " build", "s": 7.5, "e": 7.78}, {"w": " a", "s": 7.78, "e": 7.92}, {"w": " big", "s": 7.92, "e": 8.1}, {"w": " fire,", "s": 8.1, "e": 9.26}, {"w": " choke", "s": 9.26, "e": 9.42}, {"w": " it", "s": 9.42, "e": 9.62}, {"w": " down,", "s": 9.62, "e": 10.38}, {"w": " and", "s": 10.38, "e": 10.76}, {"w": " pour", "s": 10.76, "e": 11.04}, {"w": " white", "s": 11.04, "e": 11.34}, {"w": " smoke", "s": 11.34, "e": 11.66}, {"w": " over", "s": 11.66, "e": 12.0}, {"w": " the", "s": 12.0, "e": 12.18}, {"w": " meat", "s": 12.18, "e": 12.42}, {"w": " for", "s": 12.42, "e": 12.62}, {"w": " six", "s": 12.62, "e": 12.9}, {"w": " hours.", "s": 12.9, "e": 13.58}, {"w": " That", "s": 13.